}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
Time reversal (Eqs. 19, 32): in d = 1, with r_nu = alpha r_D, the point nu = \
alpha D, tau = alpha zeta is preserved by the flow, d_s nu = alpha d_s D and \
d_s tau = alpha d_s zeta. The second identity compares the p^4 projection of \
Gamma(1,1) with the p^2 projection of Gamma(0,2). Both hold at every qh in d \
= 1 and both fail in d = 2.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d2f0e20b-9f7d-4426-984d-c61a83b0b5bf"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
Table[d -> {ExactlyZeroQ[(ksLibrary[\"nu\", d] - al ksLibrary[\"D\", d]) /. \
ksAlphaRegulator /. ksTimeReversal],
   ExactlyZeroQ[(ksLibrary[\"tau\", d] - al ksLibrary[\"zeta\", d]) /. \
ksAlphaRegulator /. ksTimeReversal]}, {d, {1, 2}}]\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[21]:=",ExpressionUUID->"116c31e4-1404-40a3-93b9-1321e3855e8b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"1", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"True", ",", "True"}], "}"}]}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"2", "\[Rule]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"False", ",", "False"}], "}"}]}]}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.0016537531228657`*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[21]=",ExpressionUUID->"9c584164-02c8-4eca-bd2a-df4832f4fe1d"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["6. Summary", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"7ae1f488-0713-4303-9616-be7091f5790f"],

Cell["\<\
The same checks as benchmarks/KuramotoSivashinsky/run.wl and the suite hook \
tests/acceptance/KuramotoSivashinsky.wl. The last cell rebuilds the equations \
from Pipeline.wl (about 20 s, cards hidden) and checks that they are \
identical to those built above, so that this notebook and the scripted \
benchmark cannot drift apart.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5cf3960b-29c2-4031-9ad4-2cca580c0488"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
ksResults = ksChecks[];
ksSummary[ksResults]\
\>", "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[22]:=",ExpressionUUID->"6a3ca6f8-db11-4ef7-9b20-cc0f19b5a6fa"],

